    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), our premier start as he faces a soft matchup against Curry. His projection benefits significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 5.68, and even with the park penalizing him slightly, his elite batted-ball profile and position in the three-hole make him a must-start. **Kyle Tucker** (75.12) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.07) follow close behind; **Kyle Tucker** is thriving against the high xERA of Abbott, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages the high-upside matchup against Montero to offset a slight platoon disadvantage. Notably, **Jackson Merrill** (71.39) warrants a strong start today; while his SP_xERA isn't as favorable as our top trio, a massive +14% park factor boost makes him an efficient play in the five-hole.\n\nThe tightest decision on the bench involved **Tommy White** (48.09) and **Miguel Vargas** (47.27). **Tommy White** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his negative park factor and platoon disadvantage against Martinez made it difficult to justify displacing our existing starters. We are playing a cautious hand with **Nasim Nunez** (41.02); while his floor is hovering near our 40.0 threshold, his elite speed profile remains a strategic necessity for our Roto chase, even though he faces a stiff test against Wheeler.\n\nWe are monitoring the situation at the bottom of the order with **Wade Meckler** (51.82) and **Drake Baldwin** (57.37), both of whom are facing high-caliber arms in George Kirby and Imanaga respectively. **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s efficiency is propped up by his batting order, but owners should be wary of Imanaga\u2019s ability to suppress production. Aside from **Andy Pages**, who remains sidelined on the IL, our roster health is stable. We will look to **Henry Bolte** to provide a spark at the top of the order, relying on his +10% order bonus to counteract a difficult park environment.",
